== 1 the two shapes of a <Canvas> markup cannot write ==
-- a bare <Canvas />
   refused: <Canvas /> is not a tag you write — a shape IS the canvas. Put <Rectangle />, <Ellipse />, <Path /> or <ResourceImage /> where you wanted the canvas, inside a <Box> that gives it a size
-- a <Canvas> with a shape inside it
   refused: <Canvas> holds 1 children and lays nothing out — and nesting a shape is not how a canvas is drawn. Drop the <Canvas> and write the shape itself inside a <Box>

== 2 and the form that draws ==
-- the shape itself, inside a <Box>
   mounted

ok the bare refusal does not ask for a nested shape
ok it names the tag to write instead
ok it says the shape replaces the canvas
ok the nested refusal says to drop the <Canvas>
ok and the working form raises nothing
